module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_coproduct_declares_one_variant_twice

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { BlockerClassUnstated, RecurringFailureMode, RungUnread }

data a_coproduct_declares_one_variant_twice: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "a_coproduct_declares_one_variant_twice" as NonEmptyStr,
  rung: RungUnread { cause: BlockerClassUnstated },

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: one coproduct declaration names the same variant twice. One name, two declarations, in a single type -- the section 3 single-authority defect stated at the grain where the substrate can see it, and distinct from two variants sharing a leaf name under DIFFERENT containment, which is a namespace-identity question and not this row.",
    "HARM: lookup by exact authored name takes the first match and never asks whether a second exists, so the duplicate is not merely tolerated, it is unobservable. Every consumer resolves to the first declaration and the second is dead vocabulary that still reads as declared. Nothing downstream can distinguish the two, so no consumer can report the defect either; the declaration is degenerate and the whole pipeline answers as though it were not.",
    "RECEIPT, AND IT IS A LIVE ONE RATHER THAN A CONSTRUCTED SPECIMEN: extdeps.systemd SystemdUnitProperty carried two identical SubState declaration arms and two identical wire arms, on origin/main since gunbc#9761 and gunbc#10443, through every required run in that window without a single diagnostic. It was surfaced only when v1.compiler.infer_patterns find_variant_child_keyed began keying variant lookup and refusing on more than one match: both children key equal, lookup refuses, and required-witnesses-floor and heal-generated-artifacts both refused with ChangedWitnessObservationFailed naming that declaration.",
    "POPULATION, BY INSTRUMENT RATHER THAN BY ASSERTION: an arm-level duplicate-leaf census over every coproduct declaration under dag/ and src/ -- splitting each type declaration right-hand side on its top-level pipe and counting duplicate leaf keys per declaration, rather than matching lines -- identifies the membership. SystemdUnitProperty was its sole member at the time of this receipt. The census is the reproduction route; a transcribed count is not the authority and would rot away from it.",
    "RUNG FOUND AT: mechanically preventable, and BY ACCIDENT. The refusal that caught it is a lookup-time consequence of keying variant identity for an unrelated repair, not a wall anybody built for this class. Nothing in the parser, normalize or resolve folds refuses a duplicate variant at declaration, so on any route that does not key -- which is every route before that change -- the class remains entirely silent. Reporting this as a standing mechanical prevention would be rung inflation: the mechanism is real, executes, and is enrolled, but it guards the class only where a keyed lookup happens to reach the declaration.",
    "CEILING: structurally impossible, and the argument is that the invalid state has no constructor once the declaration fold refuses it. A coproduct whose declared variant names are not distinct is not a weakly-typed program but a malformed declaration; a fold that refuses a repeated leaf at ingest leaves no accepted program in which the duplicate exists, so no validation, lookup rule or consumer discipline is needed downstream. This is a decidable, fully modeled class -- the declared children and their authored names are both in hand at the point of declaration -- so section 4b admits nothing weaker as its ceiling.",
    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, NAMING THE CAPABILITY AND NOT AN ARTIFACT: the declaration fold that constructs a Disj node refuses a declaration whose children do not carry pairwise distinct authored names, with a typed located diagnostic naming the type and the repeated name, executed on a paired probe -- a duplicate declaration refused, and a declaration whose variants merely share a prefix or differ only outside the leaf accepted. Owner unassigned at filing. A lookup-side refusal does NOT retire this row: it catches the class only where a keyed lookup reaches the declaration, which is what this receipt shows was true for years while the duplicate stood.",
    "DISPOSITION: filed from gunbc#11301, whose subject is the one-sided coverage and lookup key in v1.compiler.infer_patterns. The SystemdUnitProperty deletion landed there as a forced consequence of that PR's refusal arm, with the population measured before the edit. The declaration-time wall is deliberately NOT that PR's scope and is left to this row's trigger, so the repair that surfaced the class is not mistaken for the wall against it.",
    "CLIMB RECEIPT (gunbc#13999, merry-raven-300): the NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER has landed, and the rung it establishes is named honestly (corrected for rung inflation, per the reviews on this change). The Disj-building fold (v2.std.compilers.sugar, the two LabeledEdges fail-sites sugar_fold_coproduct_pipe_chain and sugar_separated_rhs_as_coproduct_otherwise) now refuses a type declaration whose children do not carry pairwise distinct authored names, with a TYPED LOCATED diagnostic -- reason ^sugar_reason_duplicate_variant_name, at a declaration_locus naming the type and the name declared twice -- not the generic ^sugar_reason_malformed over a bare node locus. The enclosing type name is read from the type_decl's parse shell and threaded down the normalize recursion (a Node carries no parent pointer; precedent: under_fn_decl), so the fold at the type_decl's type_alias_rhs can name the declaration. RUNG REACHED: structurally guaranteed (rung 3), on the parse/normalize route -- the compiler now derives a refusal from modeled structure (the declaration's own children and their authored names), so no Accepted program produced by parsing and normalizing a top-level type declaration contains the duplicate. It is NOT structurally impossible: the source can still describe type T = A | A (the probe parses that exact source and hands it to the compiler), so the state still has a constructor in the canonical model, and other Disj construction routes -- the v1 seed, and any route that builds a Disj node without passing through these two v2 normalize folds -- can still reach it; the rung 4 ceiling is therefore NOT claimed. It is likewise not merely mechanically preventable: the wall is a fold-stage compiler refusal derived from structure, not an enrolled test, lens or gate whose execution safety must be preserved. NOT COVERED, stated rather than implied: the v1 seed and any Disj construction route that does not pass through these two folds, and a keyed lookup-side refusal, which still does NOT retire this row (it catches the class only where a keyed lookup reaches the declaration). NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER (to reach the rung 4 ceiling): refuse the duplicate on the remaining Disj construction routes -- the v1 seed and the parse layer -- so that a duplicate-variant Disj has no constructor in the canonical model; until then rung 3 on the parse/normalize route is the honest ceiling this change establishes, and this is the highest rung its executed evidence supports. Executing evidence (the paired probe v2.test.claim.parse.coproduct_variant_duplicate, run by claim_batch on BuildBuddy; the .dag is read at runtime, so the RED/GREEN flip needed no rebuild): RED (pre-fix) duplicate_variant_duplicate_name_is_refused_with_a_typed_located_diagnostic FAILs -- the refusal exists but is only ^sugar_reason_malformed / NodeLocus, so the typed ^sugar_reason_duplicate_variant_name + DeclarationLocus assertion fails -- while the positive control prefix_shared_variant_names_are_accepted (type T = A | AB, variants sharing only a prefix, distinct names) PASSES, so the wall is not over-broad. GREEN (with this change) both PASS, and the duplicate refusal names the type T and the repeated name A. The probe stays as the permanent regression control; the production handling (the silent acceptance) on the parse/normalize route is discharged; this row is the evidence and stays updated.",
    "CLIMB RECEIPT REWORK (gunbc#13999 review round, merry-raven-300): two findings on this change were fixed, and neither moves the rung. (a) MEANING FORK, CLOSED: the duplicate diagnostic's no-repeat arm carried ^sugar_reason_duplicate_variant_name anyway, naming a repeated variant in an edge list that repeats nothing -- a fabricated subject (section 5) and a second reason for a materially different contract (section 3). That arm now keeps sugar_malformed_diagnostic, so the duplicate reason is reachable only where a repeated authored name was actually read; the cause is decided once by edges_conform(children, LabeledEdges) at the two fail-sites instead of re-derived after the fact. The fold cannot itself emit the unnamed case -- sugar_variant_to_disj_edge mints Authored names and refuses a nameless arm before the LabeledEdges check, and v2.std.node_query variant_declaration_edge_optional yields an edge only for an Authored label -- so the arm is pinned by calling the diagnostic AT ITS OWN INTERFACE with edge lists the fold cannot produce: distinct positional edges report ^sugar_reason_malformed, authored repeated edges report ^sugar_reason_duplicate_variant_name at a DeclarationLocus naming T and A. (b) QUADRATIC COPY, REMOVED: the per-edge label_occurrences rescan -- O(n^2), and a second decision of what all_names_distinct already decides -- is gone; the repeated name now comes from v2.std.node_query repeated_authored_name_optional, which reuses the one existing O(n) Map scan (repeated_name_edges) so a single pass answers both questions (section 2, no re-invention; section 6, bare minimum cost). It sits beside that scan rather than beside all_names_distinct because v2.std.node keeps its measured census without Optional/first/Map, and importing them there moves the tree-wide unimported-bare-provider census floor (the note beside v2.std.node first_edge_read). EXECUTING EVIDENCE for the rework (same probe v2.test.claim.parse.coproduct_variant_duplicate, claim_batch on BuildBuddy, .dag read at runtime): GREEN -- all five claims PASS: duplicate_variant_duplicate_name_is_refused_with_a_typed_located_diagnostic, prefix_shared_variant_names_are_accepted, unnamed_variant_is_refused_as_malformed_not_as_duplicate (public route: type T = { x: Int } | B refused, and NOT with the duplicate reason), distinct_but_unnamed_edges_are_not_reported_as_a_duplicate_variant, repeated_authored_edge_is_reported_as_a_typed_located_duplicate_variant. RED (production at the pre-rework commit, the new probe kept): distinct_but_unnamed_edges_are_not_reported_as_a_duplicate_variant FAILs -- the old arm reported a duplicate where nothing repeated -- while its pair repeated_authored_edge_is_reported_as_a_typed_located_duplicate_variant PASSES, which is what makes the pair discriminating: it pins WHICH branch carries WHICH reason rather than that some refusal happens. RUNG UNCHANGED at structurally guaranteed (rung 3) on the parse/normalize route; the rung 4 ceiling and its next-rung trigger stand as received above.",
  ],
  evidence: [],
}
